# Calculating parameter $alpha_{k}$ in "Geometric structure of the Metropolis process in MCMC sampling for a normal distribution by the flatness of the $\alpha$-connection"

## Overview
This repository contains the Mathematica code for the paper: "Geometric structure of the Metropolis process in MCMC sampling for a normal distribution by the flatness of the $\alpha$-connection".

## Requirements
- Mathematica / Wolfram Language (Version 10.0)
- Windows 11

## Directory Structure
This repository is organized by calculation conditions. Each folder contains a main package and a subsequent script that should be executed afterward.

```text
.
├── Folder "Section 6.1"/                    # Calculation for Cases (A), (B) and (C) in Section 6.1
│   ├── Folder "Case A"/             # Folder for Calculation Condition (A)
│   │   ├── KY_calculation_alpha_case_A.wl    # 1st: Main calculation package for $\alpha_{k}$
│   │   └── KY_calculation_alpha_case_A_for_generating_Figures.wl    # 2nd: Subsequent generating figures script
│   ├── Folder "Case B"/             # Folder for Calculation Condition (B)
│   │   ├── KY_calculation_alpha_case_B.wl       # 1st: Main calculation package for $\alpha_{k}$
│   │   └── KY_calculation_alpha_case_B_for_generating_Figures.wl # 2nd: Subsequent generating figures script
│   ├── Folder "Case C"/             # Folder for Calculation Condition (C)
│   │     ├── KY_calculation_alpha_case_C.wl       # 1st: Main calculation package for $\alpha_{k}$
│   │     └── KY_calculation_alpha_case_C_for_generating_Figures.wl # 2nd: Subsequent generating figures script
│   └── Section6_outlier.wl      # Calculation for outlier $\alpha_{k}$ in Section 6.1.1
├── Folder "Section 6.2"/                    # Calculation for Cases (D) and (E) in Section 6.2
│   ├── Folder "Case D"/             # Folder for Calculation Condition (D)
│   │   ├── KY_calculation_alpha_case_D.wl       # 1st: Main calculation package for $\alpha_{k}$
│   │   └── KY_calculation_alpha_case_D_for_generating_Figures.wl # 2nd: Subsequent generating figures script
│   └── condition4/             # Folder for Calculation Condition (E)
│       ├── KY_calculation_alpha_case_E.wl       # 1st: Main calculation package for $\alpha_{k}$
│       └── KY_calculation_alpha_case_E_for_generating_Figures.wl # 2nd: Subsequent generating figures script
├── Folder "Section 6.3"/                    # Calculation for $\alpha_{k}$ in Section 6.3
├── KY_calculation_alpha_case_A_replicated_simulation.wl        # Determine the classification accuracy, acceptance rate, and empirical distribution for $\alpha_{k}$
└── README.md
```

## Usage
To run the simulations, set your working directory to the specific condition folder first, and then load the files in order.

### General Execution Rule (Common to all conditions)
For any condition you choose, open a notebook (`.nb`) or run the following command in Mathematica to move into that directory. This allows you to load the files using just their file names:

```wolfram
(* Example: If you want to run "Section 6.1" / "Case A" *)
SetDirectory["/path/to/repository/Section 6.1/Case A"]
```

### Folder "Section 6.1":

#### Run Numerical condition (A)
```wolfram
SetDirectory["/path/to/repository/Section 6.1/Case A"]
Get["KY_calculation_alpha_case_A.wl"]       (* 1. Load Main Package *)
Get["KY_calculation_alpha_case_A_for_generating_Figures.wl"]  # (* 2. Run Subsequent Script *)
```

#### Run Calculation for outlier $\alpha_{k}$ in Section 6.1.1 under numerical condition (A)
```wolfram
SetDirectory["/path/to/repository/Section 6.1"]
Get["Section6_outlier.wl"]       (* Load Main Package *)
```

#### Run Numerical condition (B)
```wolfram
SetDirectory["/path/to/repository/Section 6.1/Case B"]
Get["KY_calculation_alpha_case_B.wl"]       (* 1. Load Main Package *)
Get["KY_calculation_alpha_case_B_for_generating_Figures.wl"] # (* 2. Run Subsequent Script *)
```

#### Run Numerical condition (C)
```wolfram
SetDirectory["/path/to/repository/Section 6.1/Case C"]
Get["KY_calculation_alpha_case_C.wl"]       (* 1. Load Main Package *)
Get["KY_calculation_alpha_case_C_for_generating_Figures.wl"] # (* 2. Run Subsequent Script *)
```
---

### Folder "Section 6.2":

#### Run Numerical condition (D)
```wolfram
SetDirectory["/path/to/repository/Section 6.2/Case D"]
Get["KY_calculation_alpha_case_D.wl"]       (* 1. Load Main Package *)
Get["KY_calculation_alpha_case_D_for_generating_Figures.wl"]  # (* 2. Run Subsequent Script *)
```

#### Run Numerical condition (E)
```wolfram
SetDirectory["/path/to/repository/Section 6.2/Case E"]
Get["KY_calculation_alpha_case_E.wl"]       (* 1. Load Main Package *)
Get["KY_calculation_alpha_case_E_for_generating_Figures.wl"]  # (* 2. Run Subsequent Script *)
```

---

### Folder "Section 6.3": Determine the classification accuracy, acceptance rate, and empirical distribution for $\alpha_{k}$

#### Run 
```wolfram
SetDirectory["/path/to/repository/Section 6.3"]
Get["KY_calculation_alpha_case_A_replicated_simulation.wl"]       (* Load Main Package *)
```

